     <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
     <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
     <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+
+    <h2>4. Data minimization</h2>
+    <p>We collect only what is needed to provide the site. Browsing articles does not create an account, a session or a cookie. A session cookie is created only when you save an article to your reading list; it stores the list of article identifiers (at most 100) and nothing else, and it is not used for tracking.</p>
+    <p>Usernames and passwords entered on the sign-in and sign-up forms are sent over HTTPS directly to our authentication service and are not stored by this website. Those requests are sent without cookies or referrer information.</p>
+
+    <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
+    <ul>
+      <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> (fonts.googleapis.com, fonts.gstatic.com): serves the headline font; your IP address is transmitted to Google when it loads.</li>
+      <li><strong>Authentication service</strong> (us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net): processes sign-in and registration requests when you submit those forms.</li>
+      <li><strong>Analytics</strong> (same host): loaded only if you click “Accept” in the privacy banner. It is never loaded if your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control. You can change your choice by clearing this site’s local storage.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <p>Third-party services are reviewed before they are added and periodically afterwards, and the list above is updated whenever it changes. The site’s Content Security Policy only permits connections to the services listed here.</p>
+
+    <h2>6. Security</h2>
+    <p>The site is served over HTTPS only and sends security headers (Content-Security-Policy, Strict-Transport-Security, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy and others) to limit what browsers allow pages to load or share.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
